  "findings": [
    "The network and the Lightning module are the 1.6.1 ones apart from docstrings and the removal of the metrics mixin, so a `state_dict` loads into both with `strict=True` and the forward pass agrees at the `forward` class in eval and in train mode.",
    "The drug graphs of real molecules agree exactly (161 node features, the same one-hot layout and bond order). v2 additionally supports a molecule without bonds (deviation `graphs/single_atom_shapes`).",
    "The v2 preset (commit 174ceea7, B5) is `landmarkGenes` with `gene_list_stem: landmark_genes`, `standardize: false`, `arcsinh: false`: the 867-gene list of 1.6.1 (`DrugGNN.gene_list`) with no scaling, as in 1.6.1. Before B5 it was `landmarkGenesReduced` (270 genes). The case does not override the preset; the selected raw columns agree (`*/features_sample`).",
    "The v2 predictor defaults since B5 (174ceea7) (`epochs` 100, `batch_size` 1024) follow 1.6.1; before them they were 2 and 8. 1.6.1 uses the same `batch_size` default of 1024 for training but 32 for the validation and prediction loaders when the key is absent; v2 uses the one `batch_size` for all three (no numeric effect: the loss is averaged over the validation set with batch-size weights). The case sets all hyperparameters explicitly on both sides, and 1.6.1's `num_workers` to 0.",
    "1.6.1 early-stops on the validation loss with patience 5 and keeps the last epoch; v2 restores the best epoch (deviation `es/*`). Both early-stop only when a validation set is given; without one v2 attaches no checkpoint, so the last epoch is kept as in 1.6.1 (`no_es/*` agree).",
    "Both sides draw the shuffling permutation after the module initialization and a DataLoader base seed; with `num_workers=0` the torch RNG order is identical."
  ],
